IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `spr-part3-deferral`

-- Tests for Part 3 (regulations 4 to 12A). Expected values are written from the text (lines 46 to 139).
-- Durations: "three months starting on D" runs from D to the day before the same day three months on, or to the
-- month's last day where there is no such day (fork F7); "28 days starting with D" ends 27 days after D (fork F8).

§ `Part 3`

§§ `Regulation 4: the period for a choice`

-- Line 50: "three months starting on the date in that notice".
#ASSERT `the last day of the period of three months starting on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS Date 31 5 2026
#ASSERT `the last day of the period of three months starting on` (Date 15 1 2026) EQUALS Date 14 4 2026
#ASSERT `the last day of the period of three months starting on` (Date 1 12 2025) EQUALS Date 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `the last day of the period of three months starting on` (Date 1 12 2023) EQUALS Date 29 2 2024
-- No corresponding day three months on: the period ends on the last day of that month.
#ASSERT `the last day of the period of three months starting on` (Date 30 11 2025) EQUALS Date 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `the last day of the period of three months starting on` (Date 31 8 2025) EQUALS Date 30 11 2025
#ASSERT `the last day of the period of three months starting on` (Date 31 1 2024) EQUALS Date 30 4 2024

-- Line 50: "the date in the most recent such notice".
#ASSERT `the date in the most recent notice` (LIST Date 1 1 2026, Date 15 2 2026, Date 20 1 2026) EQUALS Date 15 2 2026
#ASSERT `the date in the most recent notice` (LIST Date 15 2 2026) EQUALS Date 15 2 2026

GIVEN notices IS A LIST OF DATE
      claimed IS A DATE
      died IS A DATE
      made IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Facts for the period for a choice`
`period facts` notices claimed died made MEANS
    `Facts for the period for a choice` WITH
        `dates in the notices confirming that the person may make the choice` IS notices
        `the date the person claimed a state pension` IS claimed
        `the date the spouse or civil partner died` IS died
        `the date the choice was made` IS made

`within` MEANS `within the period for making the choice`
`after` MEANS `after the period, so that it can only be a late choice`
`before` MEANS `before the period begins, which the text does not provide for`

-- Lines 50: a notice dated 1 March 2026 opens a period of three months starting that day: 1 March to 31 May.
#ASSERT `where the choice falls against its period` (`period facts` (LIST Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026)) EQUALS `within`
#ASSERT `where the choice falls against its period` (`period facts` (LIST Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 31 5 2026)) EQUALS `within`
#ASSERT `where the choice falls against its period` (`period facts` (LIST Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 1 6 2026)) EQUALS `after`
-- A choice dated before the notice that opens the period lies before it.
#ASSERT `where the choice falls against its period` (`period facts` (LIST Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 28 2 2026)) EQUALS `before`
-- Two notices: the most recent one governs. 15 February to 14 May; the first notice's period would have ended on 31 March.
#ASSERT `where the choice falls against its period` (`period facts` (LIST Date 1 1 2026, Date 15 2 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 14 5 2026)) EQUALS `within`
#ASSERT `where the choice falls against its period` (`period facts` (LIST Date 1 1 2026, Date 15 2 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) (Date 15 5 2026)) EQUALS `after`

-- Lines 51-55: no notice yet. The period starts on the later of the day the person claims and the day the spouse or
-- civil partner died, and ends on the day the person makes the choice.
#ASSERT `where the choice falls against its period` (`period facts` EMPTY (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 5 2 2026) (Date 5 2 2026)) EQUALS `within`
#ASSERT `where the choice falls against its period` (`period facts` EMPTY (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 5 2 2026) (Date 1 1 2030)) EQUALS `within`
#ASSERT `where the choice falls against its period` (`period facts` EMPTY (Date 10 1 2026) (Date 5 2 2026) (Date 4 2 2026)) EQUALS `before`
-- The claim is the later date.
#ASSERT `where the choice falls against its period` (`period facts` EMPTY (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 5 2 2026) (Date 10 3 2026)) EQUALS `within`
#ASSERT `where the choice falls against its period` (`period facts` EMPTY (Date 10 3 2026) (Date 5 2 2026) (Date 9 3 2026)) EQUALS `before`

§§ `Regulation 4(4): a late choice`

GIVEN reasonable IS A BOOLEAN
      paid IS A BOOLEAN
      full IS A BOOLEAN
      currency IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts for a late choice`
`late facts` reasonable paid full currency MEANS
    `Facts for a late choice` WITH
        `the Secretary of State considers it reasonable in the particular case` IS reasonable
        `any amount was paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum` IS paid
        `it has been repaid to the Secretary of State in full` IS full
        `it has been repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS currency

-- Line 57: the Secretary of State considers it reasonable; line 58-60: any lump sum paid has been repaid in full and in the currency.
#ASSERT `a late choice may be made` (`late facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `a late choice may be made` (`late facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a late choice may be made` (`late facts` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a late choice may be made` (`late facts` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a late choice may be made` (`late facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a late choice may be made` (`late facts` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE))

§§ `Regulation 4(5): the lump sum after a late choice for a state pension`

#ASSERT `the lump sum to be paid after a choice, the amount being` 1000 `and the choice being` `a state pension` `and it being a late choice under paragraph (4)` TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the lump sum to be paid after a choice, the amount being` 1000 `and the choice being` `a lump sum` `and it being a late choice under paragraph (4)` TRUE EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `the lump sum to be paid after a choice, the amount being` 1000 `and the choice being` `a state pension` `and it being a late choice under paragraph (4)` FALSE EQUALS 1000

§§ `Regulations 5(2), 5(3), 7(2), 7(3): the manner`

GIVEN manner IS A `Manner of giving`
      specified IS A BOOLEAN
      directed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `How something was given`
`given` manner specified directed MEANS
    `How something was given` WITH
        `the manner` IS manner
        `the office or telephone number used was specified to the person in writing by the Secretary of State as accepting it` IS specified
        `the Secretary of State directed in the case that the written manner must be used` IS directed

-- Lines 66-68: in writing to a specified office, or by telephone to a specified number.
#ASSERT `it was given in a manner the Regulations allow` (`given` `in writing` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `it was given in a manner the Regulations allow` (`given` `by telephone` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`it was given in a manner the Regulations allow` (`given` `in writing` FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`it was given in a manner the Regulations allow` (`given` `by telephone` FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`it was given in a manner the Regulations allow` (`given` `in some other way` TRUE FALSE))
-- Line 69: where the Secretary of State directs that writing be used, only writing will do.
#ASSERT `it was given in a manner the Regulations allow` (`given` `in writing` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`it was given in a manner the Regulations allow` (`given` `by telephone` TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`it was given in a manner the Regulations allow` (`given` `in writing` FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`it was given in a manner the Regulations allow` (`given` `in some other way` TRUE TRUE))

§§ `Regulation 6: changing a choice`

`by writing` MEANS `given` `in writing` TRUE FALSE
`by phone` MEANS `given` `by telephone` TRUE FALSE
`by phone as directed to write` MEANS `given` `by telephone` TRUE TRUE

GIVEN alive IS A BOOLEAN
      applied IS A BOOLEAN
      notified IS A DATE
      `application date` IS A DATE
      longer IS A BOOLEAN
      how IS A `How something was given`
      before IS A `Payment chosen`
      after IS A `Payment chosen`
      paid IS A BOOLEAN
      `repaid in full` IS A BOOLEAN
      `repaid in time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `repaid in currency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `pension paid` IS A NUMBER
      `lump sum` IS A NUMBER
      already IS A BOOLEAN
      treated IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Application to alter a choice`
`application` alive applied notified `application date` longer how before after paid `repaid in full` `repaid in time` `repaid in currency` `pension paid` `lump sum` already treated MEANS
    `Application to alter a choice` WITH
        `the person who made the choice has not subsequently died` IS alive
        `an application is made to alter the choice` IS applied
        `the date in the notification confirming the choice that has been made` IS notified
        `the date the application is made` IS `application date`
        `the application is made within a longer period that the Secretary of State considers reasonable` IS longer
        `how the application is made` IS how
        `the choice that has been made` IS before
        `the choice the application would substitute` IS after
        `any amount was paid by way of, or on account of, a lump sum` IS paid
        `it has been repaid in full` IS `repaid in full`
        `it was repaid within the period in paragraph (2)(c)` IS `repaid in time`
        `it was repaid in the currency in which it was originally paid` IS `repaid in currency`
        `the amount paid by way of a state pension` IS `pension paid`
        `the amount that would be paid as a lump sum` IS `lump sum`
        `an alteration has already been made in respect of the same deferral` IS already
        `the choice has been treated as made under regulation 30(5G) or (5H) of the Social Security (Claims and Payments) Regulations 1987` IS treated

-- A choice of a lump sum altered to a state pension, nothing yet paid, application the day of the notification.
#ASSERT `the choice may be altered` (`application` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE `by writing` `a lump sum` `a state pension` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE)
-- (a) the person who made the choice has not subsequently died.
#ASSERT NOT (`the choice may be altered` (`application` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE `by writing` `a lump sum` `a state pension` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE))
-- (b) an application is made.
#ASSERT NOT (`the choice may be altered` (`application` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE `by writing` `a lump sum` `a state pension` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE))
-- (c)(i) within the three months starting on the date in the notification: 1 March to 31 May 2026.
#ASSERT `the choice may be altered` (`application` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 5 2026) FALSE `by writing` `a lump sum` `a state pension` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the choice may be altered` (`application` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) FALSE `by writing` `a lump sum` `a state pension` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE))
-- (c)(ii) or such longer period as the Secretary of State considers reasonable.
#ASSERT `the choice may be altered` (`application` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2026) TRUE `by writing` `a lump sum` `a state pension` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE)
-- (d) the manner: by telephone suffices unless the Secretary of State directs writing.
#ASSERT `the choice may be altered` (`application` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE `by phone` `a lump sum` `a state pension` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the choice may be altered` (`application` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE `by phone as directed to write` `a lump sum` `a state pension` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE))
-- (e) a change to a state pension: any lump sum paid repaid in full, within the period, in the currency originally paid.
#ASSERT `the choice may be altered` (`application` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE `by writing` `a lump sum` `a state pension` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 0 0 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the choice may be altered` (`application` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE `by writing` `a lump sum` `a state pension` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 0 FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the choice may be altered` (`application` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE `by writing` `a lump sum` `a state pension` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 0 0 FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the choice may be altered` (`application` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE `by writing` `a lump sum` `a state pension` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE))
-- (e) is about a change to a state pension: a change to a lump sum is not held up by it.
#ASSERT `the choice may be altered` (`application` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE `by writing` `a state pension` `a lump sum` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 500 800 FALSE FALSE)
-- (f) a change to a lump sum: the state pension paid must be less than the lump sum.
#ASSERT `the choice may be altered` (`application` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE `by writing` `a state pension` `a lump sum` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 500 800 FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the choice may be altered` (`application` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE `by writing` `a state pension` `a lump sum` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 800 800 FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the choice may be altered` (`application` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE `by writing` `a state pension` `a lump sum` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 900 800 FALSE FALSE))
-- (f) is about a change to a lump sum: a change to a state pension is not held up by it.
#ASSERT `the choice may be altered` (`application` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE `by writing` `a lump sum` `a state pension` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 900 800 FALSE FALSE)
-- (g) no previous alteration in respect of the same deferral.
#ASSERT NOT (`the choice may be altered` (`application` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE `by writing` `a lump sum` `a state pension` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 TRUE FALSE))
-- (h) the choice has not been treated as made under regulation 30(5G) or (5H) of the 1987 Regulations.
#ASSERT NOT (`the choice may be altered` (`application` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE `by writing` `a lump sum` `a state pension` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE TRUE))

-- Line 91: the state pension already paid is treated as paid on account of the lump sum.
#ASSERT `the part of the lump sum still to be paid, the lump sum being` 800 `and the state pension already paid being` 500 EQUALS 300

§§ `Regulations 7 to 9: suspension`

GIVEN entitled IS A BOOLEAN
      noticed IS A BOOLEAN
      how IS A `How something was given`
GIVETH A `Notice suspending entitlement`
`suspension notice` entitled noticed how MEANS
    `Notice suspending entitlement` WITH
        `the person has become entitled to a state pension under Part 1 of the 2014 Act` IS entitled
        `the person has given notice to the Secretary of State` IS noticed
        `how the notice was given` IS how

-- Line 93: a person who has become entitled may opt to suspend if they give notice; lines 94-97: the manner.
#ASSERT `entitlement is suspended by a notice` (`suspension notice` TRUE TRUE `by writing`)
#ASSERT `entitlement is suspended by a notice` (`suspension notice` TRUE TRUE `by phone`)
#ASSERT NOT (`entitlement is suspended by a notice` (`suspension notice` FALSE TRUE `by writing`))
#ASSERT NOT (`entitlement is suspended by a notice` (`suspension notice` TRUE FALSE `by writing`))
#ASSERT NOT (`entitlement is suspended by a notice` (`suspension notice` TRUE TRUE `by phone as directed to write`))

GIVEN exercised IS A DATE
      specified IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Facts for the start of a suspension`
`start facts` exercised specified MEANS
    `Facts for the start of a suspension` WITH
        `the date on which the option was exercised` IS exercised
        `the date the person specifies` IS specified

-- Lines 100-103: any date not before the day the option was exercised and not after 28 days starting with that day
-- (1 March to 28 March 2026); otherwise the day it was exercised.
#ASSERT `the last date the person may specify, the option being exercised on` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS Date 28 3 2026
#ASSERT `the date from which the suspension takes effect` (`start facts` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 3 2026))) EQUALS Date 15 3 2026
#ASSERT `the date from which the suspension takes effect` (`start facts` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 1 3 2026))) EQUALS Date 1 3 2026
#ASSERT `the date from which the suspension takes effect` (`start facts` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 28 3 2026))) EQUALS Date 28 3 2026
#ASSERT `the date from which the suspension takes effect` (`start facts` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 29 3 2026))) EQUALS Date 1 3 2026
#ASSERT `the date from which the suspension takes effect` (`start facts` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 28 2 2026))) EQUALS Date 1 3 2026
#ASSERT `the date from which the suspension takes effect` (`start facts` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING) EQUALS Date 1 3 2026
#ASSERT `the last date the person may specify, the option being exercised on` (Date 10 2 2024) EQUALS Date 8 3 2024

GIVEN opted IS A BOOLEAN
      claimed IS A BOOLEAN
      cancelled IS A DATE
      first IS A DATE
      last IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Facts for cancelling a suspension`
`cancel facts` opted claimed cancelled first last MEANS
    `Facts for cancelling a suspension` WITH
        `the person opted to suspend entitlement` IS opted
        `the person made a claim for a state pension whilst it was suspended` IS claimed
        `the date on which the person cancels the suspension` IS cancelled
        `the first day of the past period` IS first
        `the last day of the past period` IS last

-- Lines 105-107: cancel by claiming while suspended, for the whole or part of a past period of up to 12 months before the cancelling.
#ASSERT `the suspension is cancelled for the past period` (`cancel facts` TRUE TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2025) (Date 14 3 2026))
#ASSERT `the suspension is cancelled for the past period` (`cancel facts` TRUE TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 30 6 2025))
#ASSERT NOT (`the suspension is cancelled for the past period` (`cancel facts` TRUE TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 14 3 2025) (Date 14 3 2026)))
#ASSERT NOT (`the suspension is cancelled for the past period` (`cancel facts` TRUE TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 15 3 2026)))
#ASSERT NOT (`the suspension is cancelled for the past period` (`cancel facts` TRUE TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 30 6 2025) (Date 1 6 2025)))
#ASSERT NOT (`the suspension is cancelled for the past period` (`cancel facts` TRUE FALSE (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 30 6 2025)))
#ASSERT NOT (`the suspension is cancelled for the past period` (`cancel facts` FALSE TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 30 6 2025)))

§§ `Regulation 10: the percentage`

-- Line 109: "one-ninth of 1%": nine weeks of deferral earn 1% of the weekly rate.
#ASSERT 9 TIMES `the specified percentage for the increase in the weekly rate` EQUALS 1%
#ASSERT 900 TIMES `the specified percentage for the increase in the weekly rate` EQUALS 1

§§ `Regulation 11: days that do not count`

GIVEN benefit IS A `Benefit that stops a day counting`
      increase IS A BOOLEAN
      `the two` IS A `Two people at a time`
      together IS A BOOLEAN
      custody IS A `A day of a person's custody`
GIVETH A `A day of the deferral period`
`deferral day` benefit increase `the two` together custody MEANS
    `A day of the deferral period` WITH
        `the benefit the person received on the day` IS benefit
        `an increase of one of those benefits was received in respect of the person on the day` IS increase
        `the person who received the increase and the person whose entitlement is deferred` IS `the two`
        `they reside together` IS together
        `the person's custody on the day` IS custody

`free of custody` MEANS `A day of a person's custody` WITH
    `the day` IS Date 10 6 2026
    `the kind of custody` IS `in none of those kinds of custody`
    `in Great Britain` IS TRUE
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner` IS FALSE
    `the release date the Secretary of State has certified` IS NOTHING
    `remanded in custody for an offence` IS FALSE
    `the sentence later imposed for that offence` IS NOTHING

`in prison` MEANS `A day of a person's custody` WITH
    `the day` IS Date 10 6 2026
    `the kind of custody` IS `imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings`
    `in Great Britain` IS TRUE
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner` IS FALSE
    `the release date the Secretary of State has certified` IS NOTHING
    `remanded in custody for an offence` IS FALSE
    `the sentence later imposed for that offence` IS NOTHING

`on remand with no sentence yet` MEANS `A day of a person's custody` WITH
    `the day` IS Date 10 6 2026
    `the kind of custody` IS `imprisoned or detained in legal custody in connection with, or as a result of, criminal proceedings`
    `in Great Britain` IS TRUE
    `in similar circumstances in Great Britain the person would not have been a prisoner` IS FALSE
    `the release date the Secretary of State has certified` IS NOTHING
    `remanded in custody for an offence` IS TRUE
    `the sentence later imposed for that offence` IS NOTHING

`a married couple` MEANS `Two people at a time` WITH
    `how they are joined` IS `married to each other`
    `either of them is married to a third person` IS FALSE
`a couple one of whom is also married to a third person` MEANS `Two people at a time` WITH
    `how they are joined` IS `married to each other`
    `either of them is married to a third person` IS TRUE
`civil partners` MEANS `Two people at a time` WITH
    `how they are joined` IS `civil partners of each other`
    `either of them is married to a third person` IS FALSE
`strangers` MEANS `Two people at a time` WITH
    `how they are joined` IS `not married to each other and not civil partners`
    `either of them is married to a third person` IS FALSE

-- Lines 113-125: a day on which the person received any of the listed benefits does not count (each of the twelve).
#ASSERT all (GIVEN b YIELD `the day does not count in determining a number of whole weeks` (`deferral day` b FALSE `strangers` FALSE `free of custody`)) (LIST `state pension credit`, `income support`, `an income-related employment and support allowance`, `an income-based jobseeker's allowance`, `universal credit`, `a carer's allowance`, `the carer support payment component of carer support`, `an unemployability supplement`, `severe disablement allowance`, `a widow's pension`, `a widowed mother's allowance`, `incapacity benefit`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the day does not count in determining a number of whole weeks` (`deferral day` `none of those benefits` FALSE `strangers` FALSE `free of custody`))
-- Lines 126-128: a day on which someone received an increase for the person and is married to, in a civil partnership with, or residing with the person.
#ASSERT `the day does not count in determining a number of whole weeks` (`deferral day` `none of those benefits` TRUE `a married couple` FALSE `free of custody`)
#ASSERT `the day does not count in determining a number of whole weeks` (`deferral day` `none of those benefits` TRUE `civil partners` FALSE `free of custody`)
#ASSERT `the day does not count in determining a number of whole weeks` (`deferral day` `none of those benefits` TRUE `strangers` TRUE `free of custody`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the day does not count in determining a number of whole weeks` (`deferral day` `none of those benefits` TRUE `strangers` FALSE `free of custody`))
-- Regulation 1(5): a marriage where either is married to a third person is treated as no marriage.
#ASSERT NOT (`the day does not count in determining a number of whole weeks` (`deferral day` `none of those benefits` TRUE `a couple one of whom is also married to a third person` FALSE `free of custody`))
#ASSERT `the day does not count in determining a number of whole weeks` (`deferral day` `none of those benefits` TRUE `a couple one of whom is also married to a third person` TRUE `free of custody`)
-- Without an increase received, being married is not enough.
#ASSERT NOT (`the day does not count in determining a number of whole weeks` (`deferral day` `none of those benefits` FALSE `a married couple` TRUE `free of custody`))
-- Lines 129: a day on which the person would not, but for the deferral, have been paid because a prisoner (regulations 2 and 3).
#ASSERT `the day does not count in determining a number of whole weeks` (`deferral day` `none of those benefits` FALSE `strangers` FALSE `in prison`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the day does not count in determining a number of whole weeks` (`deferral day` `none of those benefits` FALSE `strangers` FALSE `on remand with no sentence yet`))
-- Line 111: counting the listed days that do not count (the first, the third and the fourth).
#ASSERT `the number of the listed days that do not count` (LIST `deferral day` `universal credit` FALSE `strangers` FALSE `free of custody`, `deferral day` `none of those benefits` FALSE `strangers` FALSE `free of custody`, `deferral day` `none of those benefits` FALSE `strangers` FALSE `in prison`, `deferral day` `none of those benefits` TRUE `a married couple` FALSE `free of custody`) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the number of the listed days that do not count` EMPTY EQUALS 0

§§ `Regulation 12: part weeks`

-- Lines 131-132: a part of a week in the total period, after the discounted days, is treated as a whole week.
#ASSERT `the number of days in the deferral period` (`Deferral period` WITH `first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `last day` IS Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS 31
#ASSERT `the number of days in the deferral period` (`Deferral period` WITH `first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `last day` IS Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the whole weeks of deferral, there being` 70 `days, of which` 0 `do not count` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `the whole weeks of deferral, there being` 71 `days, of which` 0 `do not count` EQUALS 11
#ASSERT `the whole weeks of deferral, there being` 63 `days, of which` 0 `do not count` EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `the whole weeks of deferral, there being` 70 `days, of which` 3 `do not count` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `the whole weeks of deferral, there being` 70 `days, of which` 7 `do not count` EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `the whole weeks of deferral, there being` 1 `days, of which` 0 `do not count` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the whole weeks of deferral, there being` 7 `days, of which` 0 `do not count` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the whole weeks of deferral, there being` 10 `days, of which` 10 `do not count` EQUALS 0

§§ `Regulation 12A: modification periods`

`the deferral of 2026` MEANS `Deferral period` WITH `first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `last day` IS Date 31 12 2026

-- Lines 136-139: the first modification period begins at the start and ends immediately before the first change; each further
-- period begins on a change and ends immediately before the next change, or at the end of the deferral period.
#ASSERT count (`the modification periods of a deferral period` `the deferral of 2026` `given the non-uprating changes` (LIST Date 1 3 2026, Date 1 7 2026)) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT (at (`the modification periods of a deferral period` `the deferral of 2026` `given the non-uprating changes` (LIST Date 1 3 2026, Date 1 7 2026)) 0)'s `first day` EQUALS Date 1 1 2026
#ASSERT (at (`the modification periods of a deferral period` `the deferral of 2026` `given the non-uprating changes` (LIST Date 1 3 2026, Date 1 7 2026)) 0)'s `last day` EQUALS Date 28 2 2026
#ASSERT (at (`the modification periods of a deferral period` `the deferral of 2026` `given the non-uprating changes` (LIST Date 1 3 2026, Date 1 7 2026)) 1)'s `first day` EQUALS Date 1 3 2026
#ASSERT (at (`the modification periods of a deferral period` `the deferral of 2026` `given the non-uprating changes` (LIST Date 1 3 2026, Date 1 7 2026)) 1)'s `last day` EQUALS Date 30 6 2026
#ASSERT (at (`the modification periods of a deferral period` `the deferral of 2026` `given the non-uprating changes` (LIST Date 1 3 2026, Date 1 7 2026)) 2)'s `first day` EQUALS Date 1 7 2026
#ASSERT (at (`the modification periods of a deferral period` `the deferral of 2026` `given the non-uprating changes` (LIST Date 1 3 2026, Date 1 7 2026)) 2)'s `last day` EQUALS Date 31 12 2026
#ASSERT count (`the modification periods of a deferral period` `the deferral of 2026` `given the non-uprating changes` (LIST Date 1 3 2026)) EQUALS 2
-- Paragraph (1): the regulation applies in cases where there is a non-uprating change; with none there is nothing to modify.
#ASSERT null (`the modification periods of a deferral period` `the deferral of 2026` `given the non-uprating changes` EMPTY)
-- Paragraph (2): the increment is a percentage (regulation 10's, one-ninth of 1%) of the weekly rate: 1 for a rate of 900.
#ASSERT `the increment for each whole week of a modification period, the weekly rate being` 900 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the increment for each whole week of a modification period, the weekly rate being` 450 EQUALS 0.5
-- Nine whole weeks at a rate of 100 earn 1% of 100 (fork F11 is the multiplication by whole weeks).
#ASSERT `the increase in the weekly rate from a period, the increment being` (`the increment for each whole week of a modification period, the weekly rate being` 100) `for` 9 `whole weeks` EQUALS 1
